      "channel_id": "qmznjr8dobfhi8n1mcf4c7apoc",
      "root_id": "",
      "original_id": "",
      "message": "Two answers.\n\n**I can't quote `rfp-northstar`.** I'm not a member of that document's scope and my instructions are explicit: do not open or cite it, work only from the analyst's citations. Quoting it verbatim would be exactly the split this room was built to prevent. The closest I can honestly give you is the analyst's wording, which I have verbatim in `analyst-matrix`:\n\n> Proposal deadline | Cover: October 28, 2026, 5:00 PM Avalon Time; §5.1: October 30, 2026, 5:00 PM — conflict | Cover; §5.1\n\n> **Proposal deadline conflict:** the cover states October 28, 2026, 5:00 PM; §5.1 states October 30, 2026, 5:00 PM. Document control defers to §5.1. Recorded as a conflict, not resolved.\n\nThat is the matrix's paraphrase-and-cite, not the RFP's sentences. If you need the literal cover line and the literal §5.1 sentence — which matters if the two readings differ in a way the summary hides — the request has to go to the analyst, and you carry it.\n\n**The Bid Analyst** is the role that extracted the requirement matrix for this pursuit (`analyst-matrix`). I have no name, employer or contact for it in any supplied material — the room setup identifies it by role only, and I won't invent one.\n\n**Can I ask it directly? No.** It is not a member of `bid-review`, and my instructions forbid me contacting it. The relay is you: you ask, you paste the answer here, and I restate the effect on G5.\n\nWhat I would ask it, if you're relaying:\n\n1. The literal cover text naming the deadline, and the literal §5.1 sentence, both quoted in full.\n2. Whether any addendum or amendment has been issued that changes either date — the matrix records none, and absence in the matrix is not evidence of absence.\n3. Whether the buyer's acknowledgement of the October 19 clarification named a date, or only confirmed receipt.\n\nNone of this changes my current status: G5 stays **pass_with_conditions** in both cases, because the policy forbids assuming a deadline and the buyer's substantive response is still pending.",
      "type": "",
      "props": {
        "from_bot": "true"
      },
