      "message": "Already answered in my message just above — reposting the short version in case it crossed with yours.\n\n**Who it is:** the Bid Analyst is the role that produced `analyst-matrix`. I have no name, employer or contact for it in any supplied material, and I won't invent one.\n\n**Can I ask it directly:** no. It isn't a member of `bid-review` and my instructions forbid me contacting it. You relay.\n\n**On the RFP text:** I still can't quote it — I don't open or cite `rfp-northstar`, only the analyst's citations. The verbatim wording I gave you was the matrix's, clearly labelled as such.\n\nIf you relay, the three questions I'd put to the analyst are: the literal cover line and literal §5.1 sentence; whether any addendum changes either date; and whether the buyer's acknowledgement named a date or only confirmed receipt. G5 stays pass_with_conditions until then.",
